#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""omacvm-gestures (guest side): replays the Mac trackpad's multi-finger
gestures on a virtual touchpad, so libinput/Hyprland see 3/4-finger swipes and
pinch/rotate like on a real Apple touchpad; on UTM it also types the Mac's Cmd
shortcuts as Super.

Connects to the Mac helper (gestures/mac) at the Mac's address on the VM
network (/etc/omacvm/env). The helper first proves it knows the Bridge's token
("C <nonce>" from here, "M <nonce> <proof>" back, HMAC-SHA256), then this VM
does and says what it wants ("R <gestures> <glide> <proof> <name>": the feature
choices and the VM's name from the same file, the name so the Mac can tell two
VMs of one app apart). The token itself never goes over the wire, and nothing
from a listener without the proof is acted on. Then it reads lines:
  F <n> [<id> <x> <y> <size>]...   finger frame, x/y 0..1 (y down)
  S <on|off|esc> [<keys>]           capture state (esc = released by the escape combo;
                                    keys: ctrl-opt, or ctrl-opt-cmd for the old combo;
                                    none from a Mac helper before 3.0.0 = ctrl-opt-cmd)
  O <natural> <w> <h>               the Mac's scrolling direction, trackpad size (1/100 mm)
  A <dx> <dy>, W <dx> <dy>, P       scroll momentum: macOS's scroll while touching, its
                                    momentum (points), a pinch macOS recognized
  K <code> <value>                  UTM: a key on the virtual keyboard
  X <on [2]|off>                    Swipe out to macOS on or off (the Mac's setting); "2": the
                                    Mac takes such a swipe itself and follows the fingers
  N <why>                           (Mac helpers up to 3.0.18) the escape combo found no way
                                    out to macOS: ignored, no notice any more
  Q                                 the escape combo was pressed (OmacVM.app): which display is
                                    Hyprland's focused one? Answered at once with
  D <x> <y> <w> <h> | D -           where Hyprland's focused output sits on the Mac (OmacVM.app's
                                    arrangement of the VM's outputs, points, top-left origin, as
                                    the display agent got it); "-": not known (one output, another
                                    route, Hyprland not answering)
and sends, after "X on 2":
  G <n><ways>... | G -              which swipes switch workspaces (Hyprland's gestures): e.g.
                                    "G 4lr" = 4 fingers going left and right, "G -" = none;
                                    at once and after each config reload (when it can be read)
  E <l> <r>                         where a swipe of fingers going left and right goes now:
                                    left|right = out to the macOS Space on that side, - = a
                                    workspace swipe here; at once and on every workspace change
or, after "X on" (Mac helpers 3.1.0-3.1.5):
  X <left|right>                    a swipe went past the first or last workspace: out to the
                                    macOS Space on that side

Without macOS-native scroll momentum (the scroll-momentum feature; "Glide"
in the code, after the glide that follows a flick) the helper sends 3+-finger frames and 2-finger pinches; pointer,
clicks and two-finger scrolling come from the VM app's own virtual mouse.
With it (experimental) every two-finger frame comes too, and the scroll is
rebuilt here from the real fingers plus macOS's own acceleration and momentum
(docs/experiments/trackpad-scrolling.md). Runs as root (uinput). No notices
when the escape combo is used (user, 2026-10-12: "never a notice"), only once
per VM "New shortcut: ⌃⌥ Esc" when the old ⌃⌥⌘ Esc was.
"""
